k-even). Mean sigma_eff/sigma_eff(hard) across 12 (anchor, K) cells, by kernel: boundary_pair=0.999, half_int=0.999, paired_riesz=1.12, paired_triangle=1.23, paired_hann=1.23, antipair_03=2.12, antipair_05=3.24. **Decisive HARD wins** at 17 cells with p_hard_beats_kernel < 0.05: antipair_05 in 7+ cells with p<0.01 (catastrophic at K=4000, 10^9: sigma_eff = 240 vs hard 47.5, ratio 5.05×); antipair_03 at 10^9 K>=1000 with p ≈ 0.001-0.002; paired_hann/triangle at 10^9 K=1000 + 10^8 K>=2000 with p in 0.006-0.021. **Boundary-only kernels (half_int, boundary_pair) are statistically indistinguishable from hard**: max |Delta(sigma_eff/sigma_eff_hard)| = 0.6%, all 24 cells within 1-sigma noise of break-even. The head-term penalty (1-w_K)^2 Var_K = 0.25 Var_K for half_int (resp. 0.625 Var for boundary_pair) is one zero's worth of variance, swamped by the tail Sum_{j>K} Var_j ≈ K Var_K log^2 K — half a zero's variance is ~1% of total variance, below detection at N=20. **Antipair scaling matches random-phase L2 prediction exactly**: Var(antipair) - Var(hard) = (1-w)^2 K Var_avg with (1-w_k)^2 = 0.09 for antipair_03 and 0.25 for antipair_05; observed sigma_eff^2 / sigma_eff_hard^2 ratios at K=4000 are 4.5 (antipair_03) and 25.5 (antipair_05), consistent with adding 0.09 K v_avg / 0.25 K v_avg to the residual head term once K saturates the tail. **Closes the only remaining kernel-axis falsifier of the Thread 3 closure**: S196 closed log-Gaussian (multiplicative damping); S242 closed symmetric compactly-supported; S243 closes non-symmetric / paired / boundary-only / antipair. Together: HARD CUTOFF IS EMPIRICALLY L2-OPTIMAL ACROSS ALL TESTED KERNEL FAMILIES (17 kernels, 180 (anchor, K, kernel) cells across slots 3+4). **GUE pair-correlation is kernel-invariant at second-moment level**: F_GUE := sigma_eff^2 / sigma_pred^2 = 0.55 ± 0.06 across all 17 kernels (cv ≈ 11%). The L2-optimality of hard transfers verbatim to the GUE-corrected regime. **Implication for slot-1 named-exponent c