ined with Theorem A says algorithmic bound is kernel-optimal in second-moment regime). **Cross-domain ingredient**: Goldston-Montgomery 1987 bilinear-form analysis. CROSS_DOMAIN_TECHNIQUES.md entry promoted from USED-E (S195) + USED-I (S240) to USED-T (conditional theorem statement, S244). **Falsifiers**: (1) multi-sample empirical run at x >= 10^12 with sigma^2_eff exceeding (T-A) prediction by > 2x — directly tested at 10^9, sigma_eff/sigma_pred = 0.74, asymptotic correct up to GUE constant; (2) rigorous proof under just RH that gives full sigma-formula without Montgomery — would imply log^2 log K loss is unnecessary; (3) sharper pair-correlation conjecture refining (1+o(1)) to match empirical 0.55 factor — would tighten constant. **Thread 7 status**: DONE_PARTIAL_POSITIVE_CONDITIONAL. Aggregate Thread 7 contribution: polylog-time algorithm for approximate pi(x) with named-exponent error eps(x) <= sqrt(x) log log x / log^beta x for any beta > 1, conditional on RH + Montgomery's pair-correlation conjecture. Empirically verified across 3 decades (S241), kernel-optimal across 17 kernel families (S242 + S243), rigorised modulo Montgomery (S244, this slot). **First A-shape positive-direction CONDITIONAL theorem on an adjacent pi-related computation produced by the project**. **Slot self-grade**: B (rigor work; conditional theorem under unproven hypothesis; not A because Goldston-Montgomery 1987 supplies the engine; slot's contribution is the precise polylog-K specialisation, the algorithmic corollary, and the explicit valid range). **Recommended next thread**: ESCALATE TO USER — five-thread frontier fully traversed (Threads 1-4 closed per-query polylog frontier, Thread 5 closed A-grade-shaped partial-positive Correlation Dichotomy, Thread 6 closed B-NEGATIVE P1 batched-on-q, Thread 7 closed B-PARTIAL-POSITIVE-CONDITIONAL). Future commit slots should pick from OPEN_POSITIVE_TARGETS.md remaining candidates (P2 prime gap function batched on h, P4 twin-prime narrow-window,