    888	| §P.P2 batched π_h(x) on h, slot 3 — Q-truncated singular series S_Q(h) = 2 C₂ · Π_{p odd, p|h, p≤Q} (p−1)/(p−2): what is the Q at which truncation error matches σ_eff_h(x) (the "knee"), and what named-exponent formula governs the cost-vs-error tradeoff? | EXPERIMENT (B-POSITIVE: precise variance decomposition σ²_HL_Q = σ²_∞ + (1/N)·Σ_{trunc}(ε_Q·li_2)² verified at 16 (anchor, x_j, Q) cells; knee scaling Q* ≈ √x/log x with empirical match at both decades; sharp half-Gaussian shape transition Q=100→200) | E (E1.5 + S195 + S224 + S240..S244 + S418 + S419 — sharpens slot-2 cross-h-ensemble characterisation by adding the Q-axis tradeoff curve; provides the empirical foundation for slot-4 conditional-theorem wrap) | Thread 8 commit step 3/4 (S420). Built `experiments/analytic/batched_pi_h/slot3_q_truncation.py` (~370 lines): 26-h ensemble with max-prime-factor spanning [3, 2003] (slot-2 set + 18 additions covering h=2p for p ∈ {19, 23, 29, 31, 41, 53, 79, 109, 151, 199, 251, 401, 503, 599, 1009, 2003} plus mixed h=606=2·3·101 and h=3030=2·3·5·101) × 9 Q-values {30, 50, 100, 200, 500, 1000, 2000, 5000, ∞} × 2 anchors x ∈ {10⁷, 10⁸} × 5 log-uniform x_j in quarter-decade. Single 16s run, 260 raw rows + 90 cross-h aggregates + 26 truncation rows + 10 knee rows. **Headline: named-exponent variance decomposition** σ²_HL_Q(x, h-ensemble) = σ²_∞(x, h-ensemble) + (1/N) · Σ_{h: max_p_h > Q} (ε_Q(h) · li_2(x))² where ε_Q(h) = |S_∞(h) − S_Q(h)|. Empirical-vs-predicted comparison at 16 (anchor, x_j, Q) cells: 5–25% of σ_emp across all cells, closest at and above the knee. Decomposition is intrinsic-noise (slot-2's σ_∞) + h-deterministic truncation, treated as quadrature-additive (mild anti-correlation observed at low Q). **Knee scaling Q* ≈ √x/log x** verified at both anchors: x=10⁷ empirical knee_Q=200, knee_max_p=199 (predicted √x/log x = 196); x=10⁸ empirical knee_Q ∈ {1000, 2000}, knee_max_p ∈ {599, 1009} (predicted 543, off-grid between 500/1000). Knee defined as smallest Q with σ_HL_Q ≤ 1.05·σ_HL_∞. **Sharp half-Gaussian shape transition Q=100 → Q=200**: cross-h KS median p_eff jumps from 0.0015 (Q=100, 0/10 cells pass p>0.1) to 0.96 (Q=200, 10/10 cells pass), tracking the σ-knee. Below the knee, truncation contamination dominates intrinsic noise and breaks the slot-2 half-Gaussian profile; above the knee, cross-h shape recovers across all 10 cells. **σ_HL_Q values across (anchor, x_j, Q)**: at x=10⁷, σ drops from 638→446→357→174→168→171→172→173→173 across Q={30, 50, 100, 200, 500, 1000, 2000, 5000, ∞}; at x=10⁸, 5163→3615→2996→528→441→419→405→409→409. Plateau at Q ≥ 2000 (all max_p_h in our set ≤ 2003). **Per-h cost dimension**: S_Q(h) by trial division costs min(Q, √h) odd integers tested. For h_max=4006, full S_∞ is 31 steps, Q=30 is 15 steps (50% saving). Average cost across 26-h ensemble: 7.0 (Q=30) → 8.5 (Q=∞), 18% saving. **Q-truncation gives no asymptotic cost saving in original P2 polylog regime** (h ≤ poly log x ⇒ √h ≤ poly log x ≤ Q* = √x/log x); knee Q* is *algebraic* in x, not polylog. **What this rules out**: (i) Q-truncation as an algorithmic novelty for original P2 — knee Q* is asymptotically larger than √h_max in the polylog-h regime; (ii) the hypothesis that σ_HL_Q decreases monotonically with Q across all measured Q (no plateau) — directly REJECTED, clean knee at Q=200/1000-2000; (iii) the hypothesis that σ_HL_Q at Q = max_p_h(h_set) exceeds σ_HL_∞ by > 10% — directly REJECTED, σ_HL_5000 = σ_HL_∞ exactly at 5 decimal places. **What this does NOT close**: (i) conditional theorem rigorising the variance decomposition — slot 4 (4a) target; (ii) third-decade scaling validation at x=10⁹ — slot 4 (4b) candidate; (iii) worst-case (per-h) tail bound — half-Gaussian-shape implies √(log N) worst-case scaling but not formally derived; (iv) effective constant F (slot-2's 0.36-0.70) as part of the named exponent — packaged in (1+o(1)). **Cross-domain ingredient**: same as Goldston-Montgomery 1987 bilinear-form decomposition